==============================
  TradeSupport — Docker Guide
==============================

REQUIREMENTS
------------
- Docker Desktop must be installed and running


CONFIGURATION
-------------
All environment variables are managed in a single file at the project root:

    .env

The file is divided into three sections:

    # --- Frontend ---
    VITE_API_BASE_URL
    VITE_WS_URL

    # --- Backend ---
    OPENAI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ...
    ALLOWED_ORIGINS
    SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_PASSWORD, ...
    JWT_SECRET_KEY, ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRES_MINUTES, REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_DAYS

    # --- Database ---
    POSTGRES_DB, POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, POSTGRES_HOST, POSTGRES_PORT
    PGADMIN_DEFAULT_EMAIL, PGADMIN_DEFAULT_PASSWORD, PGADMIN_PORT

See .env.example for a full reference.


COMMANDS
--------
Start the app:
    docker compose up --build

Start in background:
    docker compose up --build -d

Stop the app:
    docker compose down

Stop and delete all data (including volumes):
    docker compose down -v

View logs (all services):
    docker compose logs -f

View logs for a specific service:
    docker compose logs -f backend
    docker compose logs -f frontend
    docker compose logs -f postgres
    docker compose logs -f pgadmin

Rebuild a single service:
    docker compose up -d --build backend
    docker compose up -d --build frontend


TESTING
-------
Backend unit tests (from backend/testing/):
    pytest -m unit

Frontend tests (from frontend/):
    npm test


URLS
----
Frontend  → http://localhost:5173
Backend   → http://localhost:8000
pgAdmin   → http://localhost:5050  (admin@admin.com / admin)
